<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24505" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inter-vallo</span></b> , āre, v.
			a.
		vallum, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to take</i> or <i>assume at
			intervals</i> (post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">intervallando potestates assiduas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 27, 11</span></i>
			. — Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">intervallātus</span></b> , a, um, P.
				a., <i>separated</i>, <i>having
				intervals</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">febris,</span>”
				<i>intermittent fever</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Gell.
					1, 12</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">intervallato brevi tempore,</span>”
				<i>after a short time</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 26, 1, 3</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
